  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Vista del Camino — also known as Shelly Sharpe Memorial — is one of the most-played courses in the Phoenix metro, a Scottsdale public course that dates to 1984. Four pin layouts stretch it from 4,723 feet to a 7,250-foot marathon, all at par 54.",
    "Free to play with concrete tees and Chainstar baskets, it's very cart friendly and accessible at all times. Three small lakes come into play on seven holes, which is what gives this open park course its teeth.",
    "A classic Scottsdale round: open, scenic, and sneakier than the par 3s suggest."
  ],
